{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqrM28niei94PdTFCPLp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing in this sitting got approved, and SR-146 is still unanchored. The verdict (`ef9d4927`, trailer `WI: WI-852`) records `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2` and `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=2`, and the pre-commit hook passed. The `exit=0` printed after the snapshot came from the `head` pipe; the snapshot itself refused.\n\n**The rework fixed every test gap from the first sitting.** Tests on a real git repository now cover `lane_commits`' three refusals (exit 2, no output file, clean tree) and exit 0 for both `review` and `file`. The empty test list, empty and missing named inputs, and the critique render's missing spec are covered too, and all 22 tests pass. The docstring no longer over-claims what the `-narrow` suffix does.\n\n**Amendment:**\n- **SR-146** changed meaning and is blessed, as last time; its cells are unchanged since then.\n- **SR-154** changed meaning and is not blessed. The new Requirement adds the attended trigger, but only labels the logging and rework clauses \"unattended\". As written, it requires the attended path to get its reviewer from the agent registry, with consent on and from a different family, from \"a session that did not author the work\". `review_brief.py` does none of this (the launcher picks the reviewer), so the built behaviour fails the Requirement's literal text.\n\n**First approval: LLR-313 and TC-333 are returned only because of SR-154.** Their own text is blessable as written. LLR-313's filing half (`review_refusal`, `round_path`, `file_review`) only answers SR-154's amended text, and that isn't blessed yet.\n\n**Re-attestation refused, as expected.** `snapshot --reattests SR-146` refused, naming SR-154's drifted `AcceptanceCriteria` and `Requirement`, which sit in the same registry. I didn't add SR-154 to the call. There is no act commit, and the tree is clean apart from the `.requested` marker.\n\n**The follow-up:** I drafted one item in WI-852's spec `## Dispositions`, and the intake parser reads it cleanly. It is SR-154 wording only, with no code or test change: keep the routing obligation for unattended integration, and give the attended submission only a record-or-refuse obligation (or move that to SR-146). Then SR-146, SR-154, LLR-313 and TC-333 come back in one sitting. That sitting should be quick, since only SR-154's wording is left to judge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":981,"cache_read_input_tokens":399978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":981},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"messages_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":328211}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8cf33a7-067d-4b49-9e30-523229883c86","uuid":"c62a8cfb-9178-4915-b037-6666f1ed8fb7","timestamp":"2026-10-09T02:11:09.630Z","request_id":"req_011CfqrM1SMjcj2Fe6F7SMiR"}
